ram /home/lewis/tmp/vb-f1f5-final-landing-r161-20261112/session01/counters-result/ipc_frame_decode/allocations.tsv\nHOST/VARIANCE/ADVERSE OBSERVATIONS:\n# Independent R161 performance DATA review\n\nVerdict: ACCEPT limited to recorded-session MEAN comparisons for the three declared IR-interpreter metrics. All raw arithmetic, selected-session completeness and bounded provenance checks passed. This is not a causal speedup, noise-free host, individual-operation tail, generated/maxperf, release-readiness or whole-product acceptance claim. External publication proposal and packaging review remain separate.\n\nActual accepted session: /home/lewis/tmp/vb-f1f5-final-landing-r161-20261112/session01. Candidate 0530998a5636fafb32b2602c33d14b38e983f1a6; baseline 7f505d498fa35acb5b70b083ac6f02cd40f3a891 plus approved overlay 0175f57b1a63ef7a9a36c67ea0422106c7b4917d124c26944542b9383b968fed. This review uses actual new R161 session01 samples/build/preflight receipts, not retagged R131/R139 measurements. The baseline build is R139, with its own actual source/binary receipts; shared historical binary hashes are retained honestly rather than treated as newly measured samples.\n\nIndependent mean results, final-side mean rounded once to integer ps:\n\n| Metric | Baseline ps | Candidate ps | Exact-mean delta | Allowed regression |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| bench_engine_step_once_save_const_single_transition | 43094 | 38427 | -10.828529320% | 3% |\n| ipc_frame_decode | 70917 | 71548 | 0.889674826% | 5% |\n| engine_run_until_blocked_budget_10_small_workflow | 65066 | 58621 | -9.905240116% | 3% |\n\nR4 protocol version 3 SHA-256 884085f020b898a87228d73c80254480448d84d710d35675bed6efa21db1f0ce and full/build freezes verify. Predeclared plan hash verifies; exact START/COMPLETE A1/B1/B2/A2 order and all four latency phase exits are 0. Both driver logs report their complete phases, and the separate counter phase exits 0. All twelve raw latency logs/metadata/sample/estimate sets were checked: correct metric filter, 100 samples each, three-second warmup/five-second measurement, no observed operation/guard/execution failure. All 1200 samples, including outliers, remain included. Matching base/ copies agree with their own new/ files. No previous failed R161 attempt exists in the supplied session set; no historical rejected attempt or historical sample is used.\n\nArithmetic uses exact rationals parsed from the original decimal JSON tokens. Each side uses the equal-weight mean of its two original unrounded Criterion mean.point_estimate values, rounded only once to integer ps. Per-run estimates agree with all raw time/iterations sample means within floating-point serialization tolerance; supplied aggregate means, rounded values, quantiles and percent deltas agree. Unchanged canonical 3/5/3 limits are independently checked against the actual pinned perf-budget file; all integer ceilings pass. All four per-run cross-pairings are retained as observations, not extra gates or chosen subsets.\n\nAdverse observation: IPC mean rises 0.889674825649014240%, pooled p50 sample mean rises 0.608034601057133288%, and pooled p99 sample mean rises 17.487877160809949462%, from 73.089647101188332733 to 85.871474803513638465 ns. Its pooled p95 sample mean falls -0.843503887018362517%. Per-run p99: A1 p99=73.213630725694103440 ns; A2 p99=72.255787229001303163 ns; B1 p99=76.201856498752046376 ns; B2 p99=86.420308494094901862 ns. Every IPC pairing is disclosed: A1/B1 mean=0.401924539082140921%, p99=4.081515618660930704%; A1/B2 mean=0.686394853073616985%, p99=18.038550523305702679%; A2/B1 mean=1.094356739465582396%, p99=5.461250124151867946%; A2/B2 mean=1.380788932239413990%, p99=19.603303497617122662%. These upper-tail observations are not omitted or represented as improvements, and the unchanged contract applies mean ceilings rather than an invented p99 gate.\n\nP50/P95/P99 are nearest-rank quantiles of all 200 pooled Criterion sample means per side (time_ns/iterations), ranks