ransition: instructions:u=48634849591, allocation_count=13184699, bytes_allocated=233307122; ipc_frame_decode: instructions:u=31979054207, allocation_count=8425724, bytes_allocated=240019490; engine_run_until_blocked_budget_10_small_workflow: instructions:u=34771709224, allocation_count=8707684, bytes_allocated=175105068. Actual instructions:u CSV has one valid integer event row at 100.00% running for each metric; no scaled/multiplexed/missing/unsupported count is used. All histogram rows contribute count and size*count, agreeing with heaptrack's printed allocation total and supplied aggregate. The six profiler datasets have ten samples each, one-second warmup/measurement, matching metadata, actual binary/filter commands and own base/new copies. Heaptrack's debuggee command and raw compressed dataset path agree with the saved printer invocation; original stream hashes are inventoried. Commands and every raw perf/heaptrack/printer log were inspected. These are candidate-only whole filtered-process totals including startup, suite fixture setup, warmup/calibration and work, not comparative/per-operation costs. Profiler timings never enter latency calculations.\n\nHost review: all ten snapshots agree on AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D, kernel/toolchain/machine, CPU14/core/cache domain, performance governor and SMT sibling30. Idle-window attestations predate A1; premeasurement guards passed. No build/proof/profiling process appears in the saved latency/before snapshots. Ordinary desktop/model processes remain visible; CPU percentages are historical top-process snapshots, not proof of interval per-core occupancy. Whole-host latency vmstat intervals show 91\u201396% idle; swap-in occurs in every latency phase (maxima A1=132, B1=100, B2=416, A2=216); no interval swap-out is recorded. Initial since-boot vmstat rows are preserved but excluded from interval summaries. Latency CPU-pressure avg10 is zero before/after; counter completion avg10=14.60 is retained as profiling-phase pressure, n